{
  "decision": "Admit a definition on its record's declared book, with the notice for every book on the legal page (the permanent superset of #227); review only the exceptions: a record with no declared book, a declared book with no reviewed Registry notice, a hold in force or a key named here. Notice text is never invented; owner-held book texts stay owner-owed. The #227 rule is a reading of the licence, not legal advice; the owner made the legal-risk call (item 1, \"Yes, yes, yes.\").",
